1
00:02:31,069 --> 00:02:41,069
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,069 --> 00:02:45,069
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:45,069 --> 00:02:52,069
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,069 --> 00:02:59,069
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:02:59,069 --> 00:03:09,069
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, set sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,069 --> 00:03:13,069
I'm gonna be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:15,069 --> 00:03:23,069
During their journey to the New World, Luffy and his crew arrive on Fishman Island, which is located 10,000 meters below sea level.

8
00:03:23,069 --> 00:03:31,069
There, they found themselves facing the new Fishman pirates, who were looking to destroy the Ryugu Kingdom and instigated an all-out war.

9
00:03:31,069 --> 00:03:41,069
Luffy and his friends thwarted their plans, but soon became wrapped up in the affairs of another dangerous pirate, Big Mom of the Four Emperors.

10
00:03:41,069 --> 00:03:45,069
Forget Fishman Island!

11
00:03:45,069 --> 00:03:51,069
Now that you've chosen to go against me, I'll just have to get my revenge on you instead!

12
00:03:51,069 --> 00:04:03,069
Well then, Monkey D. Luffy, now that I know who you are, come here. Let's check in the New World!

13
00:04:03,069 --> 00:04:09,069
Sure thing, be there soon. I've got something I need to settle with you too.

14
00:04:09,069 --> 00:04:11,069
Hmm?

15
00:04:11,069 --> 00:04:16,069
I like this island. It's too risky to trust you with it.

16
00:04:16,069 --> 00:04:21,069
Once I get there, I'm gonna kick your ass!

17
00:04:21,069 --> 00:04:27,069
And then I'll make Fishman Island my territory!

18
00:04:31,069 --> 00:04:33,069
Little brat!

19
00:04:37,069 --> 00:04:41,069
Many problems lie ahead. A trap awaiting in the New World.

20
00:04:45,069 --> 00:04:46,069
Here.

21
00:04:46,069 --> 00:04:47,069
Oh, thanks.

22
00:04:47,069 --> 00:04:50,069
It's some of our famous kelp tea. Please give it a try.

23
00:04:50,069 --> 00:04:54,069
It helps with digestion, so it'll do you good after that big meal.

24
00:04:57,069 --> 00:05:00,069
It's great! Thanks for all the hospitality, Minister.

25
00:05:00,069 --> 00:05:04,069
Yes, you've treated us so generously. I just hope we have an inconvenience to you.

26
00:05:04,069 --> 00:05:09,069
Oh, no. There are no words to describe my gratitude for what you all have done for Fishman Island.

27
00:05:09,069 --> 00:05:10,069
This is the least I can do.

28
00:05:12,069 --> 00:05:15,069
Man, it's too bad we have to get out of here soon, huh?

29
00:05:17,069 --> 00:05:23,069
Please don't talk about leaving the island, Usopp! I'm not ready to say goodbye to you!

30
00:05:24,069 --> 00:05:26,069
Don't cry! I'm sorry, okay?

31
00:05:26,069 --> 00:05:27,069
And it's Usopp.

32
00:05:28,069 --> 00:05:30,069
Oh. Hey, where'd Frankie run off to?

33
00:05:30,069 --> 00:05:32,069
He went to figure out something with the ship earlier.

34
00:05:32,069 --> 00:05:36,069
Apparently, there's some trick he needs to learn to get us back up to the surface.

35
00:05:36,069 --> 00:05:38,069
Ugh.

36
00:05:38,069 --> 00:05:43,069
Oh, yes. This must be the list of valuables that were stolen out of the treasure chamber.

37
00:05:43,069 --> 00:05:48,069
My goodness. This is more than I thought. The tamate box, too?

38
00:05:49,069 --> 00:05:50,069
Wait, that means...

39
00:05:50,069 --> 00:05:51,069
That means I'll be the king of the ship.

40
00:05:51,069 --> 00:05:52,069
Ah!

41
00:05:53,069 --> 00:05:54,069
Oh!

42
00:05:54,069 --> 00:05:55,069
Oh!

43
00:05:55,069 --> 00:05:56,069
Oh!

44
00:05:56,069 --> 00:05:57,069
Oh!

45
00:05:58,069 --> 00:05:59,069
Oh!

46
00:05:59,069 --> 00:06:00,069
Oh!

47
00:06:00,069 --> 00:06:05,069
Uh!

48
00:06:05,069 --> 00:06:06,069
Straw hat. Of course he'd show up. If not for him, I would be rich by now.

49
00:06:07,069 --> 00:06:10,069
Oh, well. It wasn't a total loss, at least. Still got plenty of treasure in me.

50
00:06:10,069 --> 00:06:15,829
treasure in me. Now I'll buy about a hundred pirate ships so when I get to the new world I can wipe

51
00:06:15,829 --> 00:06:27,689
out those damn straw hats. What? It's gone! How could someone steal my stolen gold? I can't even afford

52
00:06:27,689 --> 00:06:36,349
a piece of candy to soothe my sorrows now! My dear, sweet, precious treasure! Mark my words, I will find you!

53
00:06:40,069 --> 00:06:49,789
By the way, Jinbei, since we haven't spoken in some time, might you tell me how the Sun Pirates are faring?

54
00:06:49,789 --> 00:06:54,949
Quite well. In fact, they have so much energy I can scarcely keep up with them sometimes.

55
00:06:54,949 --> 00:07:00,709
Hmm. If I may be perfectly frank with you, I never imagined that the Sun Pirates would

56
00:07:00,709 --> 00:07:09,109
align themselves with Big Mom. I was quite taken aback by the news, but perhaps that is my ignorance speaking.

57
00:07:10,069 --> 00:07:15,909
Do you believe it's a wise decision? Big Mom is ruthless, but she lets us do as we please.

58
00:07:15,909 --> 00:07:23,189
It's fine for now. Hmm. I see. Then if I may be frank once more, it surprises me that you're

59
00:07:23,189 --> 00:07:29,349
comfortable taking orders from anyone other than Fish or Tiger. No, it's alright. I'm not above

60
00:07:29,349 --> 00:07:35,189
working under someone else's authority by any means. That's the way it works in the new world. If a

61
00:07:35,189 --> 00:07:41,029
captain wishes to guarantee the safety of his crew, allying with the four emperors is the best way to do it.

62
00:07:41,029 --> 00:07:49,029
Is that all? It seems to me that you're doing it for the good of Fishman Island as well. Even after

63
00:07:49,029 --> 00:07:55,109
Whitebeard's passing, our kingdom remains safe under Big Mom's protection because you connected us with

64
00:07:55,109 --> 00:08:02,149
her. We can't thank you enough for that, Jinbei. Oh no. Please don't thank me. We have a responsibility

65
00:08:02,149 --> 00:08:07,349
to make sure Fishman Island is protected. Even if we are wanted criminals.

66
00:08:10,549 --> 00:08:17,829
Having said that, I believe that the time may have come for me to terminate my partnership with Big Mom.

67
00:08:17,829 --> 00:08:21,109
Ah, so you're going to accept Luffy's invitation.

68
00:08:23,189 --> 00:08:29,749
Hey, Jinbei. What do you say, pal? Will you join my crew?

69
00:08:31,509 --> 00:08:38,869
Yes. I have made my decision. But the pirate world operates through honor, not contracts.

70
00:08:38,869 --> 00:08:43,749
We'd much rather make a verbal agreement over drinks than sign documents. Because of that,

71
00:08:43,749 --> 00:08:49,429
we mustn't go breaking such agreements without careful consideration. What concerns me the most

72
00:08:49,429 --> 00:08:53,429
is the possibility that Big Mom will direct your anger at Fishman Island.

73
00:08:57,429 --> 00:09:01,829
Honestly, Jinbei. You need not feel responsible for every little thing.

74
00:09:01,829 --> 00:09:13,669
If such an incident comes to pass, then so be it. I have a plan. Why, just today we took in 70,000

75
00:09:13,669 --> 00:09:21,429
fierce newcomers from Fishman District. They'll make fine soldiers. Do not worry about us, Jamal.

76
00:09:21,429 --> 00:09:31,989
And in the event we lose the protection of Big Mom's Jolly Roger, there is another flag I'd like to use instead.

77
00:09:33,989 --> 00:09:38,069
One with a straw hat might look nice, don't you think, Jamal?

78
00:09:40,069 --> 00:09:43,349
Couldn't agree more. I'm partial to that flag myself.

79
00:09:43,349 --> 00:09:48,229
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.

80
00:09:50,229 --> 00:09:51,669
Your Majesty!

81
00:09:52,949 --> 00:09:56,389
Forgive me, but we have a serious problem.

82
00:09:56,389 --> 00:09:56,949
Hm?

83
00:09:57,829 --> 00:09:58,869
It's terrible.

84
00:09:58,869 --> 00:10:01,589
