171
00:14:06,429 --> 00:14:09,069
What makes that punk think he can pick a fight with Mama?

172
00:14:09,489 --> 00:14:12,329
Mais oui, the monsieur does have a certain je ne sais quoi.

173
00:14:12,829 --> 00:14:14,669
She must be furious, sir.

174
00:14:14,669 --> 00:14:16,769
The tea party's in four days.

175
00:14:17,529 --> 00:14:20,609
I say we get her as many treats as we can on the way back.

176
00:14:20,869 --> 00:14:24,089
We can't fix it, but hopefully we can soften the blow.

177
00:14:24,369 --> 00:14:25,489
At least a little bit.

178
00:14:25,769 --> 00:14:26,149
Indeed.

179
00:14:26,629 --> 00:14:32,169
Hopefully a detente will be adequate, and I am sure the treasures won't hurt.

180
00:14:32,589 --> 00:14:33,269
I knew it!

181
00:14:33,349 --> 00:14:34,189
Those are mine!

182
00:14:34,189 --> 00:14:36,469
Just wait till I catch you two!

183
00:14:36,929 --> 00:14:38,429
I'll bury you alive!

184
00:14:39,189 --> 00:14:41,229
I stole those treasures once!

185
00:14:41,549 --> 00:14:43,589
That means I can steal them again!

186
00:14:44,849 --> 00:14:45,249
Pardon?

187
00:14:45,709 --> 00:14:47,689
I feel like I've seen that ugly mug before.

188
00:14:48,169 --> 00:14:48,609
Get out!

189
00:14:49,909 --> 00:14:50,889
There he is!

190
00:14:51,689 --> 00:14:53,229
It says here he's an up-and-comer.

191
00:14:53,409 --> 00:14:55,189
Goes by the name Wet-Head Caribou.

192
00:14:55,509 --> 00:14:55,889
Get out!

193
00:14:56,149 --> 00:14:56,489
Oh!

194
00:14:57,009 --> 00:14:58,569
So he's worth 200 million!

195
00:14:59,009 --> 00:14:59,449
Great!

196
00:14:59,689 --> 00:15:01,169
Just when we thought this was over!

197
00:15:01,329 --> 00:15:02,049
He he he!

198
00:15:02,049 --> 00:15:04,969
It's too late for you to beg for mercy!

199
00:15:08,509 --> 00:15:10,729
Swamp, swamp, cat Lincoln!

200
00:15:22,329 --> 00:15:23,649
Sorry, boys!

201
00:15:23,789 --> 00:15:26,209
That's what happens when you steal from me!

202
00:15:32,049 --> 00:15:36,509
This is crazy!

203
00:15:38,509 --> 00:15:53,509
He he he he!

204
00:15:53,509 --> 00:15:59,969
He he he he he!

205
00:15:59,969 --> 00:16:00,969
He he he he he!

206
00:16:00,969 --> 00:16:01,969
He he he he!

207
00:16:01,969 --> 00:16:02,969
Huh?

208
00:16:02,969 --> 00:16:03,969
Wait, what?

209
00:16:03,969 --> 00:16:04,969
Huh?

210
00:16:04,969 --> 00:16:05,969
A turtle?

211
00:16:05,969 --> 00:16:11,849
A turtle?

212
00:16:11,849 --> 00:16:12,429
A turtle?

213
00:16:12,429 --> 00:16:22,309
A turtle?

214
00:16:24,809 --> 00:16:25,349
They are here!

215
00:16:25,609 --> 00:16:26,629
He he he he he!

216
00:16:26,629 --> 00:16:27,709
A turtle?

217
00:16:27,789 --> 00:16:29,389
A turtle?

218
00:16:29,389 --> 00:16:30,149
A tank?

219
00:16:30,329 --> 00:16:30,749
What?

220
00:16:30,749 --> 00:16:31,729
What?

221
00:16:31,749 --> 00:16:32,489
What?

222
00:16:32,489 --> 00:16:32,949
What?

223
00:16:32,949 --> 00:16:33,929
Oh!

224
00:16:33,929 --> 00:16:34,889
A little big tiger!

225
00:16:34,889 --> 00:16:36,229
Who cares?

226
00:16:37,669 --> 00:16:39,669
You don't scare me!

227
00:17:04,889 --> 00:17:17,629
People with low-gear double fruit powers always end up dying young.

228
00:17:17,629 --> 00:17:20,129
You fools think that power makes you invincible.

229
00:17:20,549 --> 00:17:21,029
Gidda!

230
00:17:21,569 --> 00:17:24,029
Half-ball challenges are très disappointing.

231
00:17:25,249 --> 00:17:26,989
Allons-y, monsieur Pecum's.

232
00:17:28,349 --> 00:17:29,369
Mama's waiting.

233
00:17:30,309 --> 00:17:34,529
That guy's worth 200 million, and he just...

234
00:17:34,529 --> 00:17:38,789
