242
00:18:18,089 --> 00:18:23,889
I can't wait.

243
00:18:32,829 --> 00:18:37,109
And somewhere near the Red Line, in the waters of the New World.

244
00:18:37,109 --> 00:18:37,909
We're seeing you.

245
00:18:43,549 --> 00:18:44,769
Merchant report from headquarters.

246
00:18:45,229 --> 00:18:47,929
Several coded ships are ascending from the seafloor at high speed.

247
00:18:49,189 --> 00:18:50,909
All hands distinctions now.

248
00:18:51,089 --> 00:18:53,929
I repeat, everyone get to your posts quickly!

249
00:18:53,929 --> 00:19:15,389
That's a pirate ship!

250
00:19:23,929 --> 00:19:44,929
There's another one at two o'clock!

251
00:19:44,929 --> 00:19:48,929
Fire ships are popping up all over the place, sir!

252
00:19:48,929 --> 00:19:51,929
What the hell is this?

253
00:19:53,929 --> 00:20:06,929
Trying to get on our good side, you suck-up?

254
00:20:06,929 --> 00:20:09,929
Mind your own business!

255
00:20:09,929 --> 00:20:12,929
They finally set me free from that living hell!

256
00:20:12,929 --> 00:20:14,929
I can't die now!

257
00:20:14,929 --> 00:20:17,929
Here comes the big one!

258
00:20:17,929 --> 00:20:19,929
Captain, look out!

259
00:20:19,929 --> 00:20:22,929
I'll shield you from harm, Captain!

260
00:20:22,929 --> 00:20:23,929
Get out of the way!

261
00:20:23,929 --> 00:20:24,929
I want to do it!

262
00:20:24,929 --> 00:20:25,929
Move!

263
00:20:25,929 --> 00:20:29,929
I've got it!

264
00:20:37,929 --> 00:20:38,929
Woo!

265
00:20:38,929 --> 00:20:40,929
That's our captain for ya!

266
00:20:40,929 --> 00:20:42,929
That was really beautiful, Captain!

267
00:20:42,929 --> 00:20:45,929
Yeah, and the swordplay wasn't half bad either!

268
00:20:45,929 --> 00:20:49,929
Are you taking this seriously or not?

269
00:20:49,929 --> 00:20:52,929
Every one of you should know how to deflect a bombshell!

270
00:20:52,929 --> 00:20:55,929
There was never a better time to use that skill than just now, so-

271
00:20:55,929 --> 00:20:57,929
Um, that's a mast.

272
00:20:57,929 --> 00:21:00,929
Here, I cleaned your glasses for you!

273
00:21:00,929 --> 00:21:01,929
Thank you.

274
00:21:01,929 --> 00:21:02,929
She's so cute!

275
00:21:02,929 --> 00:21:05,929
She's like a flower among this filthy crew!

276
00:21:05,929 --> 00:21:08,929
You know, I'd die for you in a heartbeat, Captain!

277
00:21:08,929 --> 00:21:09,929
Yeah, me too!

278
00:21:09,929 --> 00:21:11,929
Don't fool around in the middle of combat!

279
00:21:11,929 --> 00:21:13,929
You'll get yourselves killed!

280
00:21:13,929 --> 00:21:15,929
The G5 is such a joke!

281
00:21:15,929 --> 00:21:18,929
And to think you're all Navy soldiers!

282
00:21:18,929 --> 00:21:22,929
You had better not take me lightly just because I'm a woman!

283
00:21:22,929 --> 00:21:24,929
Oh, Captain Toshigi!

284
00:21:24,929 --> 00:21:25,929
You're just so adorable!

285
00:21:25,929 --> 00:21:27,929
How can I not respect you?

286
00:21:27,929 --> 00:21:29,929
That's exactly the kind of treatment I mean!

287
00:21:29,929 --> 00:21:32,929
There's a difference between respect and whatever you-

288
00:21:32,929 --> 00:21:33,929
Keep it down, Toshigi.

289
00:21:33,929 --> 00:21:36,929
I'm busy.

290
00:21:36,929 --> 00:21:38,929
My apologies, sir.

291
00:21:38,929 --> 00:21:40,929
I see.

292
00:21:40,929 --> 00:21:45,929
So a pirate from the seafloor named Horty Jones took you captive.

293
00:21:45,929 --> 00:21:47,929
That explains a lot.

294
00:21:47,929 --> 00:21:51,929
That must be why there were no rookies passing through Fishman Island recently.

295
00:21:51,929 --> 00:21:53,929
Took us captive?

296
00:21:53,929 --> 00:21:54,929
I wish!

297
00:21:54,929 --> 00:21:55,929
He made us his slaves!

298
00:21:55,929 --> 00:21:58,929
Horty stirred up some kind of civil war on Fishman Island!

299
00:21:58,929 --> 00:22:00,929
He made us fight for his side!

300
00:22:00,929 --> 00:22:03,929
And then this group of pirates set us free!

301
00:22:03,929 --> 00:22:05,929
A group of pirates?

302
00:22:05,929 --> 00:22:06,929
Yeah!

303
00:22:06,929 --> 00:22:07,929
But I'm not telling you who!

304
00:22:07,929 --> 00:22:09,929
Don't be stupid!

305
00:22:09,929 --> 00:22:11,929
Can't you see who we're dealing with?

306
00:22:11,929 --> 00:22:13,929
They're not just Navy soldiers!

307
00:22:13,929 --> 00:22:14,929
They're the G5!

308
00:22:14,929 --> 00:22:17,929
They use pirates as bait when they fish for sharks!

309
00:22:17,929 --> 00:22:20,929
Or even as kindling for a bonfire!

310
00:22:20,929 --> 00:22:23,929
They're the rogue unit of the Navy!

311
00:22:23,929 --> 00:22:25,929
They don't even obey orders from HQ!

312
00:22:25,929 --> 00:22:29,929
Trust me, you have no idea how ruthless these bastards are!

313
00:22:29,929 --> 00:22:35,929
Of all the people to be caught by, we had to end up in the hands of the notorious White Chase Smoker!

314
00:22:35,929 --> 00:22:44,929
Well, Vice Admiral, can we take over from here?

315
00:22:44,929 --> 00:22:46,929
No, I beg you!

316
00:22:46,929 --> 00:22:48,929
I'll tell you everything!

317
00:22:48,929 --> 00:22:49,929
Please have mercy!

318
00:22:49,929 --> 00:22:53,929
The ones who defeated Horty Jones and his crew!

319
00:22:53,929 --> 00:22:59,929
It was the Straw Hat Pirates, okay?!

320
00:22:59,929 --> 00:23:04,929
I know that already, idiot!

321
00:23:04,929 --> 00:23:12,929
Filled with both excitement and trepidation, the crew finally sets sail for the new world!

322
00:23:12,929 --> 00:23:17,929
After bidding their fond farewells, the Straw Hats leave with a new log pose in hand!

323
00:23:17,929 --> 00:23:22,929
Luffy makes a promise to the tearful Shira Hoshi and recalls an old vow he made to Shanks!

324
00:23:22,929 --> 00:23:25,929
Overcoming trials and tragedies, Luffy's dream is on course once again!

325
00:23:25,929 --> 00:23:27,929
On the next, One Piece!

326
00:23:27,929 --> 00:23:29,929
Finally time to go!

327
00:23:29,929 --> 00:23:31,929
Goodbye, Fishman Island!

328
00:23:31,929 --> 00:23:33,929
I'm gonna be King of the Pirates!

